<title>USA: 3Com Corp rescinds share buy-back program.</title>
<headline>3Com Corp rescinds share buy-back program.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CLARA, Calif 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>3Com Corp said its board voted to rescind the company's previously announced share repurchase program.</p>
<p>It said it rescinded the program because it was unclear whether such a program, under certain circumstances, would disrupt its ability to employ a pooling-of-interest accounting method when making acquisitions.</p>
<p>3Com's share repurchase program was authorized in March 1990. As of October 30, 1996, it had repurchased 24.5 million shares, with 5.5 million still to be repurchased.</p>
</text>
